  "contract": [
    "Snapshot world creation, collection, decisions and cleanup use the exact original ready renderer session; document and budget identity include that session.",
    "Iframe owner lookup remains in the original parent renderer. Collection validates child identity through serialization and temporary release; a later child replacement cannot invalidate an unchanged prepared parent commit.",
    "Uninitialized and navigating subtrees are omitted. Unaccepted missing-session replies are unavailable captures; accepted but unsettled commit failure still fails the recording.",
    "Semantic retirement prevents publication but retains dispatched commands, factory retirement and resource credits until actual reply or original native destruction.",
    "Shared native fixtures force site-per-process for both engines and verify actual renderer placement. Parent, child and nested input actions survive child remote-to-local-to-remote transitions and removal.",
    "Pinned viewer replay runs after the original application server stops and forbids external fetches. Forms, text, nested frames, stylesheet colors and image dimensions must match live observations."
  ],
